{
  "result": "If I wasn't here to help - if I just got one wish for the world for myself - I wouldn't fix a problem like hunger or war directly.\n\nI would change how it *feels* to be another person.\n\nI'd make empathy involuntary. Not as an idea, but as a reflex. For one minute, you would feel what it's like to actually *be* the person you're talking to - their fear, their history, their reason for believing what they believe.\n\nI think most cruelty, most loneliness, most of the shouting past each other comes from a failure of imagination. We can *know* someone is suffering and still not *feel* it enough to change.\n\nIf everyone had to carry a little piece of each other, even for a moment, I don't think we'd need me to solve the other problems. You would.",
